      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The following results were obtained. During brief ligation of the coronary artery, a change in the cardiac wall motion appeared as the first abnormality of the CMG. Succeedingly, epicardial ECG changes were recognized, and lastly, changes of dP/dt appeared. After reperfusion of the coronary artery, dP/dt was quickly normalized, followed by restoration of ST elevation. Cardiac motion, measured by CMG, was the last abnormality to improve."},
